Description:
   Add or update a speaker entry in the global data/speakers.yml file.
   If the speaker does not exist, it is created. If it already exists, only the
   provided fields are updated and everything else is left unchanged.
   Supports every social field defined in SpeakerSchema.

Example: Add a new speaker with several socials.
   bin/rails g speaker --name "Jane Doe" --github "janedoe" \
     --twitter "janedoe" --website "https://janedoe.example.com" \
     --bluesky "janedoe.bsky.social" --linkedin "janedoe"

Example: Update an existing speaker's socials only.
   bin/rails g speaker --name "Jane Doe" --mastodon "https://ruby.social/@janedoe"

Example: Add a speaker whose name cannot be parameterized (slug falls back to
   the GitHub handle).
   bin/rails g speaker --name "川野十行" --github "jugyo"

Example: Add aliases (alternative names) for a speaker. Each alias's slug is
   parameterized from its name. Pass multiple aliases as space-separated values.
   bin/rails g speaker --name "Jane Doe" --github "janedoe" \
     --aliases "J. Doe" "Jane Doe Smith"

Example: Add aliases to an existing speaker without touching its socials.
   bin/rails g speaker --name "Jane Doe" --github "janedoe" \
     --aliases "J. Doe"
